For an integer \(m_{\widetilde{\mathcal M}}\ge p\), an observational-law structural completion is a tuple \(\widetilde{\mathcal M}=(m_{\widetilde{\mathcal M}},Q^{\widetilde{\mathcal M}},H^{\widetilde{\mathcal M}},\xi^{\widetilde{\mathcal M}})\), where \(Q^{\widetilde{\mathcal M}},H^{\widetilde{\mathcal M}}\in\mathbb R^{m_{\widetilde{\mathcal M}}\times m_{\widetilde{\mathcal M}}}\), \(\xi^{\widetilde{\mathcal M}}\in\mathbb R^{m_{\widetilde{\mathcal M}}}\), and the endogenous equilibrium satisfies \(Q^{\widetilde{\mathcal M}}V^{\widetilde{\mathcal M}}=H^{\widetilde{\mathcal M}}\xi^{\widetilde{\mathcal M}}\). Its observed mixing matrix is
\[
 A^{\widetilde{\mathcal M}}
 =\bigl[(Q^{\widetilde{\mathcal M}})^{-1}H^{\widetilde{\mathcal M}}\bigr]_{\mathsf O,:}
 \in\mathbb R^{p\times m_{\widetilde{\mathcal M}}}.
\]
